  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Exponential growth and logarithms appear in the Passport to Advanced Math domain and in data-interpretation contexts on the EST I.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Exponent product",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( a^m\\cdot a^n=a^{m+n} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Exponent quotient",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{a^m}{a^n}=a^{m-n} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Log definition",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\log_b x = y \\Leftrightarrow b^y=x \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Log product",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\log(ab)=\\log a+\\log b \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve \\( 2^{x+1}=32 \\). \\[ 2^{x+1}=2^5 \\implies x+1=5 \\implies x=4. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "<h3>Growth and decay</h3>Exponential growth: \\( A=A_0(1+r)^t \\). Exponential decay: \\( A=A_0(1-r)^t \\). On EST I, these appear in word problems about populations, investments, or radioactive decay — identify \\( A_0 \\) (initial amount), \\( r \\) (rate), and \\( t \\) (time).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Exponentials & Logarithms",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\(\\log_b x = y \\Leftrightarrow b^y = x\\). Laws: \\(\\log(xy) = \\log x + \\log y\\); \\(\\log(x/y) = \\log x - \\log y\\); \\(\\log x^n = n\\log x\\). <strong>Exponential growth:</strong> \\(A = A_0 e^{kt}\\) (or \\(A_0 b^t\\)). Natural log: \\(\\ln(e^x) = x\\); \\(e^{\\ln x} = x\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Solving an exponential equation",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A bacteria culture starts with 500 and doubles every 3 hours. How long until there are 4000? <p>\\(4000 = 500 \\cdot 2^{t/3} \\Rightarrow 2^{t/3} = 8 = 2^3 \\Rightarrow t/3 = 3 \\Rightarrow t = 9\\) hours.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Solve \\(\\log_3(x+1) + \\log_3(x-1) = 3\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(\\log_3[(x+1)(x-1)] = 3 \\Rightarrow x^2-1 = 27 \\Rightarrow x^2 = 28 \\Rightarrow x = 2\\sqrt{7}\\) (reject negative).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
